{
  "note": "The port scope as data: what part of the FastMediaSorter checkout is watched for System Info files and string keys. Include globs, exclude entries (a reason is required) follow PORT-LEDGER 0.1 rule 5 (the Tourist Android PORT-LEDGER proposal of 2026-11-13, accepted with corrections into P:/Contracts/port-ledger/README.md). Paths are relative to the upstream root with forward slashes. The include list covers: the System Info directories (app_v2 ui/systeminfo and core/systeminfo, the noLegal diagnostics subset, wear domain/systeminfo and ui/apps/systeminfo); the System Info name patterns of the upstream wear module; the upstream files ported as System Info dependencies, one glob each; the ported tests; the System Info layouts, drawables, menu, colour and help pages, by name. A file that is rewritten on purpose is an exclusion with its reason. The noLegal source set upstream holds 96 files, of which the System Info part is the diagnostics trio; the other 93 belong to FMS_A's other sub-programs and are outside the declared scope. The strings block is this repository's addition to the contract's shape: string keys are ported by key selection and have no ledger rows, so the watch needs the prefixes (PLAN/S0018). Checked by tools/port-ledger/check-scope.ps1; items neither ported nor decided are recorded in docs/port-decisions.jsonl by tools/port-ledger/record-decision.ps1.",
  "include": [
